    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The radioactivity of any sample of the element strontium-90 decreases by $90.75\\%$ every century. Find the percentage reduction in radioactivity over each of the periods given below. (Calculate percentages correct to 3 decimal places.)",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Two centuries",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$99.144\\%$ reduction.",
          "worked": "The multiplier for each century is $1-0.9075=0.0925$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Reduction}&=(1-0.0925^2)\\times100\\%\\\\\\text{Reduction}&=99.144375\\%\\\\\\text{Reduction}&\\approx99.144\\%.\\end{align*}$$",
